        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ऊबना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ऊबना — ūbnā — \"to get bored\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रोज़ दाल खाकर अरुण ऊब गया। roz dāl khākar Aruṇ ūb gayā. Arun got bored of eating dal every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): वह ऊब गया, vah ūb gayā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ऊबना (ūbnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists Hindi ūbnā, with the sense \"to be agitated, be bewildered\", under Sanskrit údvijatē, \"is agitated\" (CDIAL 2087). The modern sense, the restless weariness of boredom, is a later turn that CDIAL does not give."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
